#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0501 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: DISCRIMINATING - the NON-wildcard analogue of STAGE-G CRITICAL 3. APERIOD is NOT declared. Shipped expression is not empty(ASPER) and var_exists(APERIOD) and empty(APERIOD), so the derived guard folds FALSE and the rule EXECUTES and stays silent. The CDISC twin (Requirements.Variables.All:[ASPER,APERIOD]) would report SKIPPED on the same data; PMDA reports a no-violation execution row instead."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col ASPER    type=Num
